          deckDescription: 'One standard 28-tile double-six domino set. Each tile has two ends showing zero to six pips; every combination from 0-0 through 6-6 appears exactly once. No playing cards or jokers; scoring is by multiples of three at layout ends.',
          suitDescription: 'Tiles are matched by pip value at the open ends of the layout. There are no traditional suits; each end value zero through six can connect to any tile sharing that value on one of its two ends.',
          rankDescription: 'There is no rank hierarchy between tiles; play legality is determined by matching the pip value at an open end. Doubles (same pips on both ends) are often played crosswise; in All Threes, ends are summed for scoring.',
